          "message": {
            "text": "The target revision removes the base revision's runtime string check for the public `q` search parameter. Express extended parsing can therefore supply an object or array to string-specific processing: object-shaped values trigger a server-side request failure, while duplicate-key arrays use element count instead of character count and bypass the intended 200-character limit before SQL construction."
          },
